      "start_seconds": 1.02,
      "end_seconds": 4.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Sorry, doctor, shall I sit here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.0,
      "end_seconds": 9.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 10.83,
      "end_seconds": 13.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.23,
      "end_seconds": 22.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.52,
      "end_seconds": 32.56,
      "duration_seconds": 9.04,
      "text": "Erm, mainly blurred vision in one eye. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.37,
      "end_seconds": 36.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.31,
      "end_seconds": 40.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Around three weeks, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 41.61,
      "end_seconds": 45.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "Mm, hm, I'd say more like a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.73,
      "end_seconds": 50.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly three to four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.65,
      "end_seconds": 56.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "Uh, yes, somewhere around that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.81,
      "end_seconds": 61.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.43,
      "end_seconds": 84.69,
      "duration_seconds": 20.26,
      "text": "Mostly mild. As for new headache at the temple, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. Oh, um, and pain when chewing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.0,
      "end_seconds": 88.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.32,
      "end_seconds": 91.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Mostly moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.86,
      "end_seconds": 95.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Did you notice any weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.74,
      "end_seconds": 100.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Definitely no weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.45,
      "end_seconds": 104.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Any fever or shoulder stiffness at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.34,
      "end_seconds": 111.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "Hmm, uh, no, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.25,
      "end_seconds": 114.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Hm, okay. So, your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.74,
      "end_seconds": 121.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, no, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.59,
      "end_seconds": 126.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.2,
      "end_seconds": 138.73,
      "duration_seconds": 10.53,
      "text": "Let me think, years back I got bad stomach cramps from erythromycin, so I stay away from it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.13,
      "end_seconds": 142.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.05,
      "end_seconds": 147.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "High cholesterol, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.18,
      "end_seconds": 158.97,
      "duration_seconds": 10.79,
      "text": "Hm, okay. Alright, high cholesterol, that matches what I have here. Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.71,
      "end_seconds": 170.04,
      "duration_seconds": 10.33,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I walk the dog every morning. I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.64,
      "end_seconds": 174.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.36,
      "end_seconds": 178.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "No surgery, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.57,
      "end_seconds": 182.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 184.56,
      "end_seconds": 188.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "It's simvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.28,
      "end_seconds": 195.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.94,
      "end_seconds": 200.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.97,
      "end_seconds": 219.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "The temporal artery is hard, tender and has no pulse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.74,
      "end_seconds": 224.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Right, all finished, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.33,
      "end_seconds": 244.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, I'd lean towards possible giant cell arteritis threatening sight."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.94,
      "end_seconds": 267.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "I'll request a temporal artery biopsy, it'll help with possible giant cell arteritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.76,
      "end_seconds": 269.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "That makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.64,
      "end_seconds": 297.96,
      "duration_seconds": 27.32,
      "text": "I want urgent blood tests done, that's for possible giant cell arteritis. You'll be taking prednisolone, 60 milligrams, once a day, until review. That should help with possible giant cell arteritis. Start the steroid today, this is to protect your sight. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.3,
      "end_seconds": 301.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Yes. I'll also refer you to the rheumatology team."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.62,
      "end_seconds": 303.32,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.36,
      "end_seconds": 311.46,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "Please come and see me tomorrow. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.93,
      "end_seconds": 317.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
